      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you should **not** double the dosage or give her a single large dose without explicit approval from her doctor, as iron toxicity can be dangerous, especially for children. High doses taken all at once can cause severe stomach upset, rectal bleeding, and even life-threatening iron overload in a single timeframe. Always follow the specific dosage instructions on the bottle and consult her healthcare provider to determine the safest and most effective way to treat her anemia and recover her energy for sports.",
